    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by the dual-threat capability of **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages**, who both benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against Sugano (4.93 xERA). **Kyle Tucker** leads the team with an elite 85.72 score, bolstered by a +19% SP skill adjustment and a 14% park factor boost. Similarly, **Andy Pages** earns a strong 75.63 rating, with his order spot at #3 providing the necessary leverage to maximize counting stats. The surprise value play remains **Drake Baldwin**, whose score of 72.03 is driven by his leadoff position (+10%) and a positive matchup against Ober; his consistent xwOBA metrics make him an essential engine for run production today.\n\nStrategic lineup construction required a difficult decision regarding **Sam Antonacci**, who was our most notable bench candidate at 39.73. Despite his potential, he fell just shy of our \"floor\" threshold of 40.0. The primary culprit for his demotion is a negative platoon split against the southpaw Imanaga and a low-leverage spot in the seventh hole, which limits his fantasy output compared to starters like **Gunnar Henderson** or **Miguel Vargas**. We are closely monitoring the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**; while he holds a respectable 51.76 score, his platoon disadvantage against Buehler warrants caution, and we are prepared to pivot to a depth piece if the weather or defensive lineups suggest a further decline in his efficiency. \n\nWe continue to navigate a depleted roster with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** sidelined on the IL, placing immense pressure on **Coby Mayo** and **Gunnar Henderson** to anchor the infield production against McClanahan. While the matchups for **Liam Hicks**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** are firmly in the \"marginal\" 50\u201354 range, their presence remains necessary to preserve our game caps while maintaining exposure to potential stolen base opportunities\u2014a category where **Gunnar Henderson** and **Miguel Vargas** must outperform their projections to keep the Waves competitive. We will continue to monitor the status of **Jacob Wilson**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Curtis Mead**, **Dominic Smith**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Luis Lara** to ensure our bench depth can adequately cover any late-inning tactical shifts or weather-related disruptions.",
